### Sample requests for every endpoint, through the gateway.
### IntelliJ IDEA: open this file and click the green ▶ next to a request (run them top to bottom the first time:
### the login requests save tokens and the create requests save ids for the requests below them).
### Start the services first: ./scripts/start-local.sh  (see docs/GETTING-STARTED.md)

@gw = http://localhost:8765

### ---------- Auth (user-service) ----------

### Log in as the seeded ADMIN -> saves {{admin}}
POST {{gw}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "rambo", "password": "password123"}

> {% client.global.set("admin", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Log in as a seeded USER -> saves {{vigo}}
POST {{gw}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "vigo", "password": "password123"}

> {% client.global.set("vigo", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Register your own user (201). Change the username if it's taken (409). -> saves {{myId}}
POST {{gw}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gaurav Pawar",
  "birthDate": "1998-04-12",
  "username": "gaurav",
  "password": "my-password-1"
}

> {% client.global.set("myId", response.body.id); %}

### Log in as yourself -> saves {{me}}
POST {{gw}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "gaurav", "password": "my-password-1"}

> {% client.global.set("me", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Who am I?
GET {{gw}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}

### ---------- Users (user-service) ----------

### All users, paged and sorted (login required)
GET {{gw}}/jpa/users?page=0&size=5&sort=name,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}

### One user
GET {{gw}}/jpa/users/{{myId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}

### Update yourself (or anyone, as ADMIN)
PUT {{gw}}/jpa/users/{{myId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Gaurav B. Pawar", "birthDate": "1998-04-12"}

### ADMIN creates a user without a login (a USER token gets 403)
POST {{gw}}/jpa/users
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Guest Author", "birthDate": "1988-01-01"}

### ---------- Posts (user-service) ----------

### Create a post as yourself -> saves {{postId}}
POST {{gw}}/jpa/users/{{myId}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"description": "Learning microservices with Spring Boot"}

> {% client.global.set("postId", response.body.id); %}

### Create several posts in one transaction (all or nothing; max 10 posts per user -> 409)
POST {{gw}}/jpa/users/{{myId}}/posts/bulk
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  {"description": "Spring Data JPA derived queries"},
  {"description": "How @Transactional rollback works"}
]

### Posts of one user (public)
GET {{gw}}/jpa/users/{{myId}}/posts

### One post (public, cached for 60 s)
GET {{gw}}/jpa/posts/{{postId}}

### Feed of all posts (public, one JOIN FETCH query)
GET {{gw}}/jpa/posts

### Same feed the slow way: watch user-service's log print 1 + N SELECTs (login required)
GET {{gw}}/jpa/posts/n-plus-one
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}

### ---------- Comments (comment-service) ----------

### Comment on your post (comment-service asks user-service whether the post exists) -> saves {{commentId}}
POST {{gw}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{vigo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"postId": {{postId}}, "text": "Great post!"}

> {% client.global.set("commentId", response.body.id); %}

### Reply
POST {{gw}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"postId": {{postId}}, "text": "Thanks for reading!"}

### Comments of a post, with the post's details from user-service (public)
GET {{gw}}/comments?postId={{postId}}

### Delete a comment: only its author or an ADMIN (204); anyone else gets 403
DELETE {{gw}}/comments/{{commentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vigo}}

### ---------- Errors on purpose ----------

### 400: banned word (rule comes from config-server)
POST {{gw}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{vigo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"postId": {{postId}}, "text": "easy scam money"}

### 404: post doesn't exist
POST {{gw}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{vigo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"postId": 999999, "text": "hello?"}

### 400: validation errors listed per field
POST {{gw}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "A", "birthDate": "2999-01-01", "username": "Bad Name!", "password": "short"}

### 401: no token
POST {{gw}}/jpa/users/{{myId}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{"description": "no token"}

### 403: posting as someone else
POST {{gw}}/jpa/users/1/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"description": "posting as rambo"}

### ---------- Clean up ----------

### ADMIN deletes your user: your posts go too (204)
DELETE {{gw}}/jpa/users/{{myId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
